{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:244deef45a542b65","name":"Wayfarer-Class Medium Transport","source":{"id":"source:reference-244deef45a542b65","title":"Wayfarer-Class Medium Transport","revision":20993,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:57:15Z","sha256":"e2f5c6800b74532cc738d036ac80dad89f76fd2071a18fdfb7793d50dbe688b7","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20993","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Wayfarer-Class%20Medium%20Transport&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-244deef45a542b65","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The unusual design of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarer"]},"-Class Medium Transport allows ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cargo Pods"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cargo_Pods?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to be attached and detached from from the port side of the vessel as needed. This modular design enables a ",{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarer"]}," to load a passenger section, hangar bay, or cargo module, depending on what is needed at the time. A ",{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarer"]}," features powerful engines that can handle the large mass of bulk freight and that gives the vessel surprising good speed. However, its unusual layout makes the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarer"]}," ungainly and difficult to pilot in anything less than ideal conditions.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The 82-meter ",{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarer"]},"-Class Medium Transport requires a crew of ten for optimal operation, but it can be flown effectively with only a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," and one other crew member. The remaining crew spend most of their time securing cargo or operating the huge docking clamps, which attach ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cargo Pods"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cargo_Pods?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to the vessel. ",{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarers"]}," are typically found around highly developed planets, such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Corellia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Corellia","referenceId":"reference:b23d752dcc50dee4"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Metellos"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Metellos?action=edit&redlink=1"},". Independent captains of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarers"]}," are virtually guaranteed to find steady, if boring, work plying the trade lanes. However, its customizable design and remarkably spacious layout makes the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarer"]}," popular with smugglers, criminals, and adventurers, who use the detachable module as a hangar for up to two Gargantuan or smaller ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Planetary Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Planetary_Vehicles"},". In a crisis, smugglers can dump their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cargo Pods"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cargo_Pods?action=edit&redlink=1"}," with the push of a button, allowing them to escape the notice of patrols and customs inspectors. Partisan and Rebel forces sometimes use Wayfarers as assault transports, landing on a planet's surface to unload ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," or troops and then quickly speeding away.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Wayfarer"]},"-Class Medium Transport Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"http